{#
   THE ADMIN LIST PAGE — one page shape for every admin list.

   `_catalogue.html.twig` did this for the public side and `_data_table.html.twig`
   did it for the table itself. This is the layer between them: the page *around*
   the table, which was still being written out by hand fifteen times.

   ⚠️ **What was actually wrong.** There were two skeletons in the codebase and
   nothing said which was current. Eleven pages used `admin-page` + `admin-layout`;
   five used `main-content` + `admin-main` + `admin-content-grid` +
   `admin-main-content` — four nested wrappers to do the job of one. Same job,
   same sidebar, different DOM, so they could never be restyled together.

   ⚠️ **The flashes were the tell.** This shell renders them; before it, one page
   styled its own success flash with a `style=""` attribute carrying a hardcoded
   green. A page that has to remember to draw its own confirmation message is a
   page that will one day forget.

   ─── S134h — the settled format ────────────────────────────────────────────

   Four rounds in `/admin/design#filtres` decided where each kind of control
   lives, and this file is where that decision is enforced for all 41 lists:

     the page header   the title, and **one green named button** for what the
                       page creates. Never an icon alone: green makes it findable,
                       the words say what it makes.
     the filter panel  `_admin_filters.html.twig` — one tile row for the facet
                       that defines the page, then "Affiner" dropdowns with
                       **sub-venue first**, the whole group gone on a
                       single-sub-venue install.
     the list header   the panel title, **the count, then the search**. Search
                       finds *one* row: it belongs to the list, not to the panel
                       of controls that decide which rows exist.

   Measured before: **394 px** of controls above the first row. After: 124 px.

   Use it with `{% embed %}`:

     {% embed 'site/_admin_list.html.twig' with {
         title: 'admin_places.title'|trans,
         description: 'admin_places.list_description'|trans,
         action_label: 'admin_places.list_action'|trans,
         action_route: 'app_admin_place_new',
         panel_title: 'admin_places.list_panel'|trans,
     } %}
         {% block content %}…the table…{% endblock %}
     {% endembed %}

   Parameters, all optional except `title`:

     title          the page heading
     description    the line under it
     action_label   the green button's words. Omitted = no button.
     action_route   where it goes
     action_params  route parameters, if it needs any
     panel_title    the heading on the panel that holds the table
     panel_note     the count line beside it, in the caller's own words
                    ("11 machine(s)") — the noun changes per list, so the shell
                    cannot write it
     list_count     rows currently shown
     list_total     rows before any filter. When it is larger than `list_count`
                    the shell replaces `panel_note` with "3 sur 11" — otherwise
                    the search box reads as if it only looked at this page.
     sidebar_variant  passed through to `_admin_sidebar` (default: standard)

   Filter panel (handed straight to `_admin_filters.html.twig`):

     list_route, list_route_params, list_query
     list_tiles, list_tiles_label, list_tiles_preserve_query
     list_refine    the "Affiner" dropdowns
     venue_context  becomes the first of them
     list_client_filter  filter in the browser instead of navigating

   Search:

     list_search_placeholder  set it and the search box appears in the list
                              header. Unset = no search.
     list_search              its current value

   Blocks:

     filters      an escape hatch for a page whose controls genuinely are not
                  facets (`/admin/reporting`'s date range). Needs `has_filters`.
     content      the table — normally an `{% embed %}` of `_data_table`
     panel_extra  anything after the table, inside the panel
     after        anything after the panel entirely

   ⚠️ This template computes NOTHING and knows what none of these things are.
   Same rule as `_catalogue`: an `{% if %}` on entity type here and it has
   stopped being a shell.
#}
{% include 'site/_header.html.twig' %}

{# ⚠️ `hero: 'compact'` (S136) renders the band the way `/admin/design#filtres`
   draws it — a short rounded strip INSIDE the content column, title and green
   button on one line — instead of the full-bleed magenta slab. The mockup was
   always the compact one; S134h put the green button into the old header and
   kept the slab, which is the half of the format that did not get applied.

   It is opt-in while the Equipment sub-menu is the trial ground. When it wins,
   the default flips and this parameter goes away — a flag that outlives its
   trial is how a codebase ends up with two heroes for good. #}
{# S140 — `hero: 'merged'` is `compact` with the seams taken out. Same three
   groups, same order, same components: the band, the filters, then the count +
   search line, then the rows. What changes is that they stop being three
   floating cards with 24 px of ground between them and become **one card** with
   dividers — the page reads as one object whose top is coloured, instead of a
   stack whose middle member happens to be a table.

   ⚠️ Nothing moves. That was the brief: the placement is already settled (S134h,
   four rounds), so this round varies ONE thing — containment — and leaves every
   control where it was. #}
{% set _merged = hero|default('') == 'merged' %}
{% set _compact_hero = hero|default('') == 'compact' or _merged %}
<main class="admin-page{{ _compact_hero ? ' has-compact-hero' : '' }}">
    {% if not _compact_hero %}
    <header class="admin-page-header">
        <div class="admin-page-header-inner">
            <div>
                <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
                {% if description|default('') %}<p>{{ description }}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {# ⚠️ **The one add button, and it is green (S134h).** It was
               `btn-primary-admin` — accent on accent, the same colour as the
               band it sits on, which is how the one thing a list page creates
               managed to be the least visible control on it.

               ⚠️ `--color-ok-fill`, not `--color-ok`. The semantic tones are
               *text* colours: `--color-ok` is `#86efac` in dark mode so the word
               "disponible" can be read on a dark panel, and filling a button
               with it gives a glaring pastel slab carrying white text at 1.7:1.
               The operator saw exactly that on 2026-08-11. #}
            {% if action_label|default('') and action_route|default('') %}
                <a class="admin-add" href="{{ path(action_route, action_params|default({})) }}">
                    <span class="admin-add-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>{{ action_label }}
                </a>
            {% endif %}
            {% block header_extra %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
    </header>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="admin-layout"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-controller="admin-list-filter"{% endif %}>
        {% include 'site/_admin_sidebar.html.twig' with {
            admin_sidebar_variant: sidebar_variant|default('standard'),
        } %}

        {# ⚠️ ONE grid item, holding both panels. `.admin-layout` is
           `260px 1fr`, so filters and table as separate children would land in
           different columns — the table would wrap back under the sidebar. #}
        <div class="admin-column">
        {# ⚠️ **The frame opens HERE when merged, and closes once at the bottom.**
           One `<section>` for the whole list — band, filters, list header, rows —
           rather than three. The two `{% if %}`s below are the same element: it
           is opened either before the hero (merged) or after the filters (the
           three-card layout), and there is exactly one `</section>` for both.
           A `{% set %}`-ed tag string would render escaped; a wrapper block would
           mean two closing tags to keep in step. #}
        {% if _merged %}<section class="admin-panel is-merged">{% endif %}
        {# The compact band, exactly as the mockup draws it: one line, the title
           left, the one green named button right, inside the column and above
           the filter panel. #}
        {% if _compact_hero %}
            <header class="admin-hero">
                <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
                {% if action_label|default('') and action_route|default('') %}
                    <a class="admin-add" href="{{ path(action_route, action_params|default({})) }}">
                        <span class="admin-add-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>{{ action_label }}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
                {% block header_extra_compact %}{% endblock %}
            </header>
        {% endif %}
        {# ⚠️ One include, no conditions. Which of the three groups render — the
           tile row, "Affiner", the sub-venue dropdown — is decided inside the
           component, by what it was given. The `if show_venue_picker or
           show_tools` ladder that used to live here is what let a page lose its
           filters the moment a second sub-venue existed.

           ⚠️ **S140 — captured rather than printed, because the two formats put
           it in different places.** Merged, the list header comes first and the
           filters sit directly above the rows they narrow; unmerged, the order
           is unchanged. Captured once and printed once either way: the
           alternative was the same fifteen-key argument hash written twice,
           which is exactly how two copies of a component start to drift.
           `{% set %}` with a body yields a `Twig\Markup`, so `{{ }}` does not
           re-escape it — no `|raw`, and no block may live inside (the list
           header's `panel_header_extra` hook is why the HEADER is not the half
           that moved). #}
        {% set _filter_group %}
            {% if list_route|default('') %}
                {% include 'site/_admin_filters.html.twig' with {
                    list_route: list_route,
                    list_route_params: list_route_params|default({}),
                    list_query: list_query|default({}),
                    tiles: list_tiles|default([]),
                    tiles_label: list_tiles_label|default(''),
                    tiles_preserve_query: list_tiles_preserve_query|default(true),
                    refine: list_refine|default([]),
                    search: list_search|default(''),
                    venue_context: venue_context|default(null),
                    client_filter: list_client_filter|default(false),
                } only %}
            {% endif %}
            {% set current_filter_chips = list_active_filters|default(workspace_filter_chips(app.request.query.all)) %}
            {% if current_filter_chips is not empty %}
                <div class="workspace-filter-chips" aria-label="{{ 'workspace.active_filters'|trans }}">
                    <span class="workspace-filter-chips-label">{{ 'workspace.active_filters'|trans }}</span>
                    {% for chip in current_filter_chips %}
                        <a class="workspace-filter-chip" href="{{ path(list_route, chip.remove_query|default({})) }}">
                            <span>{{ chip.label|default(chip.label_key|trans) }} : {{ chip.value|default('') }}</span><span aria-hidden="true">×</span><span class="sr-only">{{ 'workspace.remove_filter'|trans }}</span>
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <a class="workspace-filter-reset" href="{{ path(list_route) }}">{{ 'workspace.clear_filters'|trans }}</a>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        {% endset %}

        {% if not _merged %}{{ _filter_group }}{% endif %}

        {# The escape hatch, for controls that are not facets at all. #}
        {% if has_filters|default(false) %}
            <div class="admin-panel admin-panel-filters">
                {% block filters %}{% endblock %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if not _merged %}<section class="admin-panel">{% endif %}
            <div class="admin-panel-header">
                <h2>{{ panel_title|default(title) }}</h2>
                {# ⚠️ "3 sur 11" the moment anything narrows the list. `11
                   machine(s)` beside a search box says nothing about whether the
                   search looked past the rows on screen; the pair of numbers
                   does. `is defined` rather than `|default` — `list_total: 0` is
                   a real answer and `default` fires on empty. #}
                {% if list_total is defined and list_count is defined and list_total > list_count %}
                    <span class="admin-panel-note">{{ 'admin_list.count_of'|trans({'%count%': list_count, '%total%': list_total}) }}</span>
                {% elseif panel_note|default('') %}
                    <span class="admin-panel-note">{{ panel_note }}</span>
                {% elseif list_count is defined %}
                    {# The format says "title, count, then search" on all 41 lists, and
                       a page that never wrote itself a count sentence still owes one.
                       `panel_note` stays the override wherever the noun matters. #}
                    <span class="admin-panel-note">{{ 'admin_list.count_simple'|trans({'%count%': list_count}) }}</span>
                {% endif %}

                {# ⚠️ **Search lives here now, not in the filter panel (S134h).**
                   It is the one control that does not decide *which rows exist* —
                   it finds one among the rows that do. Sitting it beside the
                   count is what makes the count legible as a scope. #}
                {% if list_search_placeholder|default('') and list_route|default('') %}
                    <form class="admin-list-search" method="get" action="{{ path(list_route, list_route_params|default({})) }}" role="search"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-action="submit->admin-list-filter#search"{% endif %}>
                        {# ⚠️ `|filter`, not the inline `if` on a for tag — removed
                           in Twig 3. See `_admin_filters`. #}
                        {% for key, value in (list_query|default({}))|filter((value, key) => key not in ['q', 'page']) %}
                            <input type="hidden" name="{{ key }}" value="{{ value }}">
                        {% endfor %}
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg>
                        <label class="sr-only" for="admin-list-q">{{ 'common.search'|trans }}</label>
                        <input id="admin-list-q" type="search" name="q" value="{{ list_search|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ list_search_placeholder }}"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-admin-list-filter-search data-action="input->admin-list-filter#filter"{% endif %}>
                        <button class="sr-only" type="submit">{{ 'common.search'|trans }}</button>
                        {% if list_search|default('') %}<a class="admin-list-search-clear" href="{{ path(list_route, list_route_params|default({})) }}" title="{{ 'common.reset'|trans }}"><span aria-hidden="true">×</span><span class="sr-only">{{ 'common.reset'|trans }}</span></a>{% endif %}
                    </form>
                {% endif %}
                {% block panel_header_extra %}{% endblock %}
            </div>

            {# ⚠️ **Merged, the filters come after the list header** — the page
               reads title → what this list is and how many → what narrows it →
               the rows, and the filter band ends up touching the rows it acts
               on rather than being separated from them by the header. #}
            {% if _merged %}{{ _filter_group }}{% endif %}

            {# ⚠️ Emitted here, for every list, rather than left to the caller.
               `admin-flash` already carries the tone colours; a page writing its
               own is how one of them ended up with an inline hardcoded green. #}
            {% for message in app.flashes('success') %}<div class="admin-flash success">{{ message }}</div>{% endfor %}
            {% for message in app.flashes('error') %}<div class="admin-flash error">{{ message }}</div>{% endfor %}

            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
            {% block panel_extra %}{% endblock %}
        </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block after %}{% endblock %}
</main>

{# ⚠️ **The footer belongs to the shell, not to the caller.** S129 established
   that here, for the 25 pages on this list shell. S130b found the same split one
   level up — `base.html.twig` had no footer at all, so the 41 pages that do not
   come through this file ended in whitespace — and moved the include there, which
   is the only place that covers every page. This file no longer emits one;
   adding it back would render it twice. #}
